  "claim": "Scouting pass, no theorem activated. Under the canonical K1-K3 test the zero set of every nonzero trilinear form is a knot in the vector reading, and only the parity atom is one in the bit reading; every group's multiplication relation is a Latin knot, so K1-K3 does not distinguish a hard pair and pairwise versus three-way does not match not-a-knot versus knot. The #P-hard kernel count is an affine function of the number of states the vector-level knot allows, and in the signed reading pairwise phases are Gauss sums while three-place phases are #P-hard (classical). Interest 1/3; recommended against as the next epic.",
